# vfio-user

QEMU includes a `vfio-user` client. The `vfio-user` specification allows for implementing (PCI) devices in userspace outside of QEMU; it is similar to `vhost-user` but can emulate arbitrary PCI devices, not just `virtio`.

## Example

SPDK includes a virtual PCI NVMe controller implementation. Setting up a `vfio-user` UNIX socket between QEMU and SPDK:

```
--device '{"driver": "vfio-user-pci","socket": {"path": "/tmp/vfio-user.sock", "type": "unix"}}'
```

See [libvfio-user](https://github.com/nutanix/libvfio-user/) for further information.
ENDOFFILE
