# VirtIO Devices

VirtIO devices are paravirtualized devices designed to be efficient to emulate and virtualize. They are the recommended device models for virtual machines.

The [VirtIO specification](https://docs.oasis-open.org/virtio/virtio/v1.3/virtio-v1.3.html) is an open standard managed by OASIS. The device implementation can be provided wholly by QEMU, in concert with the kernel (vhost), or off-loaded to an external process via vhost user.

## Related Pages

- [[virtio-gpu]] - VirtIO GPU
- [[virtio-pmem]] - VirtIO Persistent Memory
- [[virtio-snd]] - VirtIO Sound
- [[vhost-user]] - vhost-user back ends
- [[vhost-user-contrib]] - vhost-user daemons in contrib
