# SiFive HiFive Unleashed (sifive_u)

SiFive HiFive Unleashed Development Board featuring the Freedom U540 multi-core RISC-V processor.

## Supported Devices

- 1 E51 / E31 core, Up to 4 U54 / U34 cores
- CLINT, PLIC, PRCI, L2-LIM
- DDR memory controller, 2 UARTs
- 1 GEM Ethernet controller, 1 GPIO controller
- 1 OTP memory, 1 DMA controller
- 2 QSPI controllers, 1 ISSI 25WP256 flash
- 1 SD card in SPI mode, PWM0 and PWM1

## Machine-Specific Options

- `serial=nnn` - Board serial number (default 1)
- `start-in-flash` - Jump to QSPI flash directly
- `msel=[6|11]` - Mode Select pins

## Running Linux Kernel

```bash
export ARCH=riscv
export CROSS_COMPILE=riscv64-linux-
make defconfig && make

qemu-system-riscv64 -M sifive_u -smp 5 -m 2G \
    -display none -serial stdio \
    -kernel arch/riscv/boot/Image \
    -initrd /path/to/rootfs.ext4 \
    -append "root=/dev/ram"
```

## Running U-Boot

```bash
export CROSS_COMPILE=riscv64-linux-
export OPENSBI=/path/to/opensbi-riscv64-generic-fw_dynamic.bin
make sifive_unleashed_defconfig
```

Boot from SD card (msel=11):

```bash
qemu-system-riscv64 -M sifive_u,msel=11 -smp 5 -m 8G \
    -display none -serial stdio \
    -bios /path/to/u-boot-spl.bin \
    -drive file=/path/to/sdcard.img,if=sd
```

Boot from SPI flash (msel=6):

```bash
qemu-system-riscv64 -M sifive_u,msel=6 -smp 5 -m 8G \
    -display none -serial stdio \
    -bios /path/to/u-boot-spl.bin \
    -drive file=/path/to/spi-nor.img,if=mtd
```
