# 'virt' Generic Virtual Platform (virt)

The `virt` board is a platform designed for use in virtual machines. It is the recommended board type for running Linux guests.

## Supported Devices

- Up to 512 RV32GC/RV64GC cores with optional extensions
- CLINT, PLIC, CFI parallel NOR flash
- 1 NS16550 UART, 1 Google Goldfish RTC
- 1 SiFive Test device, 8 virtio-mmio transports
- 1 generic PCIe host bridge, fw_cfg device

## Machine-Specific Options

- `aclint=[on|off]` - ACLINT vs SiFive CLINT (TCG only)
- `acpi=[on|off|auto]` - ACPI tables (default: on)
- `aia=[none|aplic|aplic-imsic]` - AIA interrupt controller
- `aia-guests=nnn` - Per-HART VS-level IMSIC pages
- `iommu-sys=[on|off]` - riscv-iommu-sys platform device

## Running Linux Kernel

```bash
export ARCH=riscv
export CROSS_COMPILE=riscv64-linux-
make defconfig && make

qemu-system-riscv64 -M virt -smp 4 -m 2G \
    -display none -serial stdio \
    -kernel arch/riscv/boot/Image \
    -initrd /path/to/rootfs.cpio \
    -append "root=/dev/ram"
```

## Running U-Boot

```bash
export CROSS_COMPILE=riscv64-linux-
make qemu-riscv64_smode_defconfig

qemu-system-riscv64 -M virt -smp 4 -m 2G \
    -display none -serial stdio \
    -kernel /path/to/u-boot.bin
```

## Using Flash Devices

Firmware images must be exactly 32 MiB. For edk2:

```bash
qemu-system-riscv64 \
   -blockdev node-name=pflash0,driver=file,read-only=on,filename=<edk2_code> \
   -blockdev node-name=pflash1,driver=file,filename=<edk2_vars> \
   -M virt,pflash0=pflash0,pflash1=pflash1
```

## Enabling TPM

```bash
swtpm socket --tpm2 -t -d --tpmstate dir=/tmp/tpm --ctrl type=unixio,path=swtpm-sock

qemu-system-riscv64 \
  -chardev socket,id=chrtpm,path=swtpm-sock \
  -tpmdev emulator,id=tpm0,chardev=chrtpm \
  -device tpm-tis-device,tpmdev=tpm0
```
