# Guest Loader

The guest loader is similar to the generic-loader but aimed at loading hypervisor guests. Useful for debugging hypervisors without firmware and boot-loaders.

The guest loader does two things:
- Load blobs (kernels and initial ram disks) into memory
- Sets platform FDT data so hypervisors can find and boot them

## Example

```
qemu-system-x86_64 -kernel ~/xen.git/xen/xen \
  -append "dom0_mem=1G,max:1G loglvl=all guest_loglvl=all" \
  -device guest-loader,addr=0x42000000,kernel=Image,bootargs="root=/dev/sda2 ro console=hvc0 earlyprintk=xen" \
  -device guest-loader,addr=0x47000000,initrd=rootfs.cpio
```

Each blob will get `/chosen/module@<addr>` entry in the FDT.

## Arguments

```
-device guest-loader,addr=<addr>[,kernel=<file>,[bootargs=<args>]][,initrd=<file>]
```

- `addr=<addr>` - Mandatory start address of the blob
- `kernel|initrd=<file>` - Filename of kernel or initrd blob
- `bootargs=<args>` - Optional kernel boot arguments

Currently supported machines: Arm and RiscV `virt` machines.
ENDOFFILE
