# Subchannel Passthrough via vfio-ccw

vfio-ccw allows making certain I/O subchannels and their devices available to a guest. The host will not interact with those subchannels/devices any more. Only ECKD DASDs have been thoroughly tested.

## Configuration Steps

### Step 1: Configure Host Device

Obtain a UUID and configure the mediated device:

```bash
uuidgen
# 7e270a25-e163-4922-af60-757fc8ed48c6

driverctl -b css set-override 0.0.0313 vfio_ccw
mdevctl define -u 7e270a25-e163-4922-af60-757fc8ed48c6 \
               -p 0.0.0313 -t vfio_ccw-io -a
```

### Step 2: Configure QEMU

```
-device vfio-ccw,devno=fe.0.1234,sysfsdev=/sys/bus/mdev/devices/7e270a25-e163-4922-af60-757fc8ed48c6
```
