# Arm Realview boards (`realview-eb`, `realview-eb-mpcore`, `realview-pb-a8`, `realview-pbx-a9`)

Several variants of the Arm RealView baseboard are emulated, including the EB, PB-A8 and PBX-A9.

Kernels for the PB-A8 board should have `CONFIG_REALVIEW_HIGH_PHYS_OFFSET` enabled and expect 512M RAM. Kernels for the PBX-A9 board should have `CONFIG_SPARSEMEM` enabled, `CONFIG_REALVIEW_HIGH_PHYS_OFFSET` disabled and expect 1024M RAM.

## Emulated devices

- ARM926E, ARM1136, ARM11MPCore, Cortex-A8 or Cortex-A9 MPCore CPU
- Arm AMBA Generic/Distributed Interrupt Controller
- Four PL011 UARTs
- SMC 91c111 or SMSC LAN9118 Ethernet adapter
- PL110 LCD controller
- PL050 KMI with PS/2 keyboard and mouse
- PCI host bridge
- PCI OHCI USB controller
- LSI53C895A PCI SCSI Host Bus Adapter with hard disk and CD-ROM devices
- PL181 MultiMedia Card Interface with SD card
