# Composable SR-IOV Device

SR-IOV (Single Root I/O Virtualization) allows a single physical function (PF) to appear as multiple virtual functions (VFs). Currently only supported by virtio-net-pci.

## Example

```bash
-netdev user,id=n -netdev user,id=o -netdev user,id=p -netdev user,id=q
-device pcie-root-port,id=b
-device virtio-net-pci,bus=b,addr=0x0.0x3,netdev=q,sriov-pf=f
-device virtio-net-pci,bus=b,addr=0x0.0x2,netdev=p,sriov-pf=f
-device virtio-net-pci,bus=b,addr=0x0.0x1,netdev=o,sriov-pf=f
-device virtio-net-pci,bus=b,addr=0x0.0x0,netdev=n,id=f
```

VFs specify the paired PF with `sriov-pf` property. The PF must be added after all VFs. Maximum 255 VFs (ARI-capable).
