# Arm System Emulator

QEMU can emulate both 32-bit and 64-bit Arm CPUs. Use `qemu-system-aarch64` for 64-bit, `qemu-system-arm` or `qemu-system-aarch64` for 32-bit.

## Choosing a Board Model

You must specify a board model with `-M` or `--machine`. For general Linux use, the `virt` board is recommended as it supports PCI, virtio, recent CPUs and large amounts of RAM.

## Board-Specific Documentation

See individual board documentation files for max78000, integratorcp, mps2, musca, realview, sbsa, versatile, vexpress, aspeed, bananapi, sabrelite, digic, cubieboard, exynos, nrf, nuvoton, imx, orangepi, raspi, stellaris, stm32, virt, vmapple, xlnx-versal, xlnx-zynq, and more.
ENDOFFILE) | depth=1
