title: "Intel Trusted Domain eXtension (TDX)"
source: "system/i386/tdx.rst"
---

# Intel Trusted Domain eXtension (TDX)

TDX extends VMX and MKTME with a new kind of VM guest called a Trust Domain (TD). A TD runs in a CPU mode that protects the confidentiality of its memory contents and CPU state from any other software, including the VMM.

## Prerequisites

Physical machine needs TDX module loaded and initialized with KVM TDX support. `KVM_CAP_VM_TYPES` will report `KVM_X86_TDX_VM` support.

### TDVF (Trust Domain Virtual Firmware)

OVMF implements TDVF support. Load with `-bios OVMF.fd`.

## Feature Configuration

Three types of configurable features:
- **Attributes**: PKS (bit 30), PERFMON (bit 63)
- **XSAVE (XFAM)**: 64-bit mask for extended features
- **CPUID**: Only some bits are directly configurable

### TDX Capabilities

Use `KVM_TDX_CAPABILITIES` command of `MEMORY_ENCRYPT_OP` ioctl.

### TD Attributes

Configure via "attributes" property of "tdx-guest" object. Individual bits: `sept-ve-disable` (bit 28).

## Launching a TD

```
qemu-system-x86_64 \
    -accel kvm \
    -cpu host \
    -object tdx-guest,id=tdx0 \
    -machine ...,confidential-guest-support=tdx0 \
    -bios OVMF.fd
```

## Restrictions

- kernel-irqchip must be split (default for TDX)
- No readonly support for private memory
- No SMM support

## Debugging

Bit 0 of TD attributes is the DEBUG bit for off-TD debug mode (future work).

## TD Attestation

Initiated by calling TDG.MR.REPORT inside TD, then converted to Quote by SGX Quoting Enclave (future work).

## References

- [TDX Homepage](https://www.intel.com/content/www/us/en/developer/articles/technical/intel-trust-domain-extensions.html)
ENDOFFILE
