title: "Independent Guest Virtual Machine (IGVM) Support"
source: "system/igvm.rst"
---

# Independent Guest Virtual Machine (IGVM) Support

IGVM files encapsulate all information required to launch a VM on any virtualization stack in a deterministic way. This allows cryptographic measurement of initial guest state for Confidential Guests.

## Overview

QEMU supports IGVM files through the `igvm-cfg` object:

```
-machine ...,confidential-guest-support=sev0,igvm-cfg=igvm0
-object sev-guest,id=sev0,cbitpos=47,reduced-phys-bits=1
-object igvm-cfg,id=igvm0,file=/path/to/sev-snp.igvm
```

## Supported Platforms

IGVM files can be provided for Confidential Guests on AMD SEV, SEV-ES and SEV-SNP with KVM, as well as non-confidential guests.

## Supported Directives

### Common (SEV, SEV-ES, SEV-SNP, non-confidential)

- `IGVM_VHT_PAGE_DATA` - NORMAL zero, measured and unmeasured page types
- `IGVM_VHT_PARAMETER_AREA`
- `IGVM_VHT_PARAMETER_INSERT`
- `IGVM_VHT_VP_COUNT_PARAMETER` - CPU count
- `IGVM_VHT_ENVIRONMENT_INFO_PARAMETER`

### Additional for SEV/SEV-ES/SEV-SNP

- `IGVM_VHT_MEMORY_MAP` - E820 table
- `IGVM_VHT_REQUIRED_MEMORY`

### Additional for SEV-ES/SEV-SNP

- `IGVM_VHT_VP_CONTEXT` - Initial CPU state via VMSA

## Initial CPU State with VMSA

For SEV-ES and SEV-SNP, initial CPU state can be defined in the IGVM file. Supported registers: RAX, RCX, RDX, RBX, RBP, RSI, RDI, R8-R15, RSP, RIP, CS, DS, ES, FS, GS, SS, CR0, CR3, CR4, XCR0, EFER, PAT, GDT, IDT, LDTR, TR, DR6, DR7, RFLAGS, X87_FCW, MXCSR.

## Firmware Images

When an IGVM filename is specified, the firmware image should be contained as a payload of the IGVM file, not provided via `-bios` or pflash.

## References

- [IGVM Project](https://github.com/microsoft/igvm)
- [buildigvm tool](https://gitlab.com/qemu-project/buildigvm)
ENDOFFILE
