# A-profile CPU architecture support

QEMU's TCG emulation includes support for Armv5, Armv6, Armv7, Armv8 and Armv9 versions of the A-profile architecture. Supported architecture extensions include:

- FEAT_AA32/AA64 (AArch32/AArch64 support)
- FEAT_AdvSIMD (Advanced SIMD Extension)
- FEAT_AES, FEAT_SHA1, FEAT_SHA256, FEAT_SHA3, FEAT_SHA512 (Crypto)
- FEAT_BTI (Branch Target Identification)
- FEAT_CRC32 (CRC32 instructions)
- FEAT_FP (Floating Point extensions)
- FEAT_FP16 (Half-precision floating-point)
- FEAT_LSE (Large System Extensions)
- FEAT_MTE (Memory Tagging Extension)
- FEAT_PAuth (Pointer authentication)
- FEAT_PMUv3 (PMU extension)
- FEAT_RAS (Reliability, availability, and serviceability)
- FEAT_RME (Realm Management Extension - experimental)
- FEAT_RNG (Random number generator)
- FEAT_SME (Scalable Matrix Extension)
- FEAT_SVE (Scalable Vector Extension)
- FEAT_SVE2 (Scalable Vector Extension v2)
- FEAT_VHE (Virtualization Host Extensions)
- FEAT_NV (Nested Virtualization)
- Many more (see source for complete list)

When a specific named CPU is being emulated, only features present in hardware for that CPU are emulated. The `max` CPU enables all features.

## R-profile CPU architecture support

QEMU's TCG emulation support for R-profile CPUs is currently limited. Only Cortex-R5 and Cortex-R5F CPUs are emulated.

## M-profile CPU architecture support

QEMU's TCG emulation includes support for Armv6-M, Armv7-M, Armv8-M, and Armv8.1-M versions of the M-profile architecture. Supported extensions:

- FP (Floating-point Extension)
- FPCXT (FPCXT access instructions)
- HP (Half-precision floating-point instructions)
- LOB (Low Overhead loops and Branch future)
- M (Main Extension)
- MPU (Memory Protection Unit Extension)
- PXN (Privileged Execute Never)
- RAS (Reliability, Serviceability and Availability)
- S (Security Extension)
- ST (System Timer Extension)

There is no equivalent of the `max` CPU for M-profile.
ENDOFFILE) | depth=1
