# Direct Linux Boot

This section explains how to launch a Linux kernel inside QEMU without having to make a full bootable image. It is very useful for fast Linux kernel testing.

## Syntax

```
qemu-system-x86_64 -kernel bzImage -drive file=rootdisk.img,format=raw -append "root=/dev/sda"
```

Use `-kernel` to provide the Linux kernel image and `-append` to give the kernel command line arguments. The `-initrd` option can be used to provide an INITRD image.

Without graphical output, redirect serial port and QEMU monitor to console:

```
qemu-system-x86_64 -kernel bzImage -drive file=rootdisk.img,format=raw \
    -append "root=/dev/sda console=ttyS0" -nographic
```

Use `Ctrl+a c` to switch between the serial console and the monitor.
ENDOFFILE
