# loongson3 virt Generic Platform (virt)

The `virt` machine uses GPEX host bridge with emulated devices such as loongson7a RTC device, IOAPIC device, ACPI device, etc.

## Supported Devices

- GPEX host bridge
- Ls7a RTC device
- Ls7a IOAPIC device
- ACPI GED device
- Fw_cfg device
- PCI/PCIe devices
- Memory device
- CPU device (type: la464)

## Boot Options

Boot by specifying UEFI BIOS, initrd, and Linux kernel.

### Build BIOS

See: https://github.com/tianocore/edk2/tree/master/OvmfPkg/LoongArchVirt#readme

### Build Kernel

```
git clone https://github.com/loongson/linux.git
cd linux
git checkout loongarch-next
make ARCH=loongarch CROSS_COMPILE=loongarch64-unknown-linux-gnu- loongson3_defconfig
make ARCH=loongarch CROSS_COMPILE=loongarch64-unknown-linux-gnu- -j32
```

### Boot Example

```
$ ./build/qemu-system-loongarch64 -machine virt -m 4G -cpu la464 \
    -smp 1 -bios QEMU_EFI.fd -kernel vmlinuz.efi -initrd ramdisk \
    -serial stdio -monitor telnet:localhost:4495,server,nowait \
    -append "root=/dev/ram rdinit=/sbin/init console=ttyS0,115200" \
    --nographic
```
