# vfio-user Protocol

> Source: `docs/interop/vfio-user.rst`

## Overview

vfio-user is a protocol that allows a device model (server) to be externalized from QEMU (client). It is based on the VFIO API, using a socket transport instead of the kernel VFIO device fd. This enables running device models in separate processes, language-agnostic device implementations, and better security isolation.

## Transport

- Uses UNIX domain sockets or TCP
- Messages framed with a header containing command, message size, flags, and version
- All multi-byte fields are little-endian

## Message Header

| Field | Size | Description |
|-------|------|-------------|
| Command | 2 bytes | Message type |
| Message Size | 4 bytes | Total message size including header |
| Flags | 2 bytes | `VFIO_USER_NO_REPLY`, `VFIO_USER_NO_STRINGS` |
| VFIO User Version | 2 bytes | Protocol version (initial: 0) |
| Migration Version | 2 bytes | Migration protocol version |
| Error | 4 bytes | Error code (0 = success) |

## Commands

| ID | Name | Description |
|----|------|-------------|
| 1 | VFIO_USER_VERSION | Negotiate protocol version |
| 2 | VFIO_USER_DMA_MAP | Register DMA memory regions |
| 3 | VFIO_USER_DMA_UNMAP | Unregister DMA memory regions |
| 4 | VFIO_USER_DEVICE_GET_INFO | Query device info (state, regions, irqs) |
| 5 | VFIO_USER_DEVICE_GET_REGION_INFO | Query region info (index, size, offset, flags) |
| 6 | VFIO_USER_DEVICE_GET_IRQ_INFO | Query interrupt information |
| 7 | VFIO_USER_DEVICE_SET_IRQS | Configure interrupts |
| 8 | VFIO_USER_REGION_READ | Read from device regions |
| 9 | VFIO_USER_REGION_WRITE | Write to device regions |
| 10 | VMSTATE_SET_UP | Set up migration |
| 11 | VMSTATE_GET_LENGTH | Get migration data length |
| 12 | VMSTATE_GET_DATA | Get migration data |
| 13 | VMSTATE_SET_DATA | Restore migration data |
| 14 | DEVICE_GET_REGION_IO_FDS | Get region I/O file descriptors |
| 15 | DEVICE_SET_LOG_BASE | Set dirty page logging base |
| 16 | DEVICE_GET_DIRTY_LOG | Get dirty page bitmap |

## Migration

The protocol supports live migration through VMSTATE commands (SET_UP, GET_LENGTH, GET_DATA, SET_DATA).

## DMA Memory Registration

- **DMA_MAP**: Register guest memory with file descriptor, offset, size, permissions
- **DMA_UNMAP**: Unregister memory regions

## Error Handling

Errors reported in the header `Error` field. Non-zero indicates failure. `NO_REPLY` flag suppresses responses.

## See Also

- VFIO API specification
- QEMU vfio-user device implementation
ENDOFFILE
