# vhost-user Protocol

> Source: `docs/interop/vhost-user.rst`

## Overview

vhost-user is a protocol for virtio device backends running in userspace. It extends the vhost protocol to work over UNIX domain sockets. QEMU acts as the slave, the device backend as the master.

## Transport

- UNIX domain sockets with SCM_RIGHTS for fd passing
- Messages use native endian

## Message Structure

| Field | Type | Description |
|-------|------|-------------|
| request | uint32_t | Message type |
| flags | uint32_t | Version (bit 2), reply flag (bit 3) |
| size | uint32_t | Payload size |

## Core Messages

| ID | Name | Description |
|----|------|-------------|
| 1 | GET_FEATURES | Get supported feature bits (64-bit bitmask) |
| 2 | SET_FEATURES | Set negotiated feature bits |
| 3 | SET_OWNER | Set current process as device owner |
| 5 | SET_MEM_TABLE | Set guest memory regions |
| 6 | SET_LOG_BASE | Set log base for dirty page tracking |
| 8 | SET_VRING_NUM | Set vring descriptor count |
| 9 | SET_VRING_ADDR | Set vring addresses |
| 10 | SET_VRING_BASE | Set vring base index |
| 11 | GET_VRING_BASE | Get vring base index (save/restore) |
| 12 | SET_VRING_KICK | Set vring kick fd |
| 13 | SET_VRING_CALL | Set vring call fd |
| 14 | SET_VRING_ERR | Set vring error fd |
| 15 | SET_PROTOCOL_FEATURES | Enable protocol feature negotiation |
| 16 | GET_PROTOCOL_FEATURES | Get supported protocol features |
| 32 | SET_VRING_ENABLE | Enable/disable a vring pair |

## IOTLB Messages

For VIRTIO_F_IOMMU_PLATFORM:

| ID | Name | Description |
|----|------|-------------|
| 22 | IOTLB_MSG | IOTLB miss/invalidate |
| 28 | IOTLB_MSG_V2 | Extended IOTLB message |

## Config and Inflight

| ID | Name | Description |
|----|------|-------------|
| 24 | GET_CONFIG | Get device config space |
| 25 | SET_CONFIG | Set device config space |
| 30 | GET_INFLIGHT_FD | Get inflight buffer fd |
| 31 | SET_INFLIGHT_FD | Set inflight buffer fd |

## Protocol Features

| Bit | Name | Description |
|-----|------|-------------|
| 0 | F_MQ | Multiple queue support |
| 1 | F_LOG_SHMFD | Shared log fd |
| 2 | F_RARP | RARP broadcasting |
| 3 | F_REPLY_ACK | Message ack support |
| 4 | F_NET_MTU | Network MTU setting |
| 5 | F_SLAVE_REQ | Slave-initiated requests |
| 9 | F_CONFIG | Config space messages |
| 12 | F_INFLIGHT_SHMFD | Inflight buffer tracking |

## Reconnection Flow

1. QEMU sends SET_OWNER
2. QEMU negotiates features
3. QEMU sets up memory table
4. QEMU configures vrings
5. Backend resumes operation

## See Also

- vhost-user-gpu protocol
- virtio specification
ENDOFFILE
