# System Emulator Targets

QEMU supports system emulation for many CPU architectures. Each target has a dedicated `qemu-system-{arch}` binary.

## Supported Targets

| Architecture | Binary | Status |
|---|---|---|
| AArch64 (ARM 64-bit) | `qemu-system-aarch64` | Full |
| ARM (32-bit) | `qemu-system-arm` | Full |
| AVR | `qemu-system-avr` | Experimental |
| Hexagon | `qemu-system-hexagon` | Experimental |
| LoongArch | `qemu-system-loongarch64` | Full |
| M68K | `qemu-system-m68k` | Full |
| MicroBlaze | `qemu-system-microblaze` | Full |
| MIPS | `qemu-system-mips` / `mipsel` / `mips64` / `mips64el` | Full |
| Nios II | `qemu-system-nios2` | Full |
| OpenRISC | `qemu-system-or1k` | Full |
| PowerPC | `qemu-system-ppc` / `ppc64` | Full |
| RISC-V | `qemu-system-riscv32` / `riscv64` | Full |
| RX | `qemu-system-rx` | Experimental |
| S390x | `qemu-system-s390x` | Full |
| SPARC | `qemu-system-sparc` | Full |
| SPARC64 | `qemu-system-sparc64` | Full |
| TriCore | `qemu-system-tricore` | Experimental |
| x86_64 | `qemu-system-x86_64` / `qemu-system-i386` | Full |
| Xtensa | `qemu-system-xtensa` | Full |

## Usage

Each target binary works the same way:

```
qemu-system-{arch} [options] [disk_image]
```

Use `-machine help` to list available machines for a target, and `-cpu help` to list supported CPUs.
